<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philip II, Duke of Pomerania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1573">1573</a>–<a href="/years/1618">1618</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Philip II of Pomerania-Stettin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philip II was duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania-stettin">Pomerania-Stettin</a> from 1606 to 1618, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-griffins">Griffin dynasty</a>. A learned collector and patron of the arts, he commissioned the Pomeranian Art Cabinet through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augsburg">Augsburg</a> agent Philipp Hainhofer and the great map of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eilhard-lubinus">Eilhard Lubinus</a>. He died childless, and the Griffin line ended with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogislaw-xiv">Bogislaw XIV</a> in 1637.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philip-ii-duke-of-pomerania.jpg" alt="Philip II, Duke of Pomerania" width="320" height="323" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unbekannter Künstler · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PhilippII.1678.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
